nd  deportation the home office a 2.5  million people now have secured digital  status and from the majority the  application process is working well but  according to this report 90%  people say they want a physical document  to prove their right to stay in the UK  rather than just relying on digital  evidence without it they say they will  feel unsettled and on Monday the House  of Lords supported that request  contradicting the government's own  advice in a move that would be welcomed  by all EU citizens who call the UK home  Charlie Angela al-jazeera London
 

